                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1500" notBefore="1400">
                        <p>15th century, origin unclear: wood boards, flush with textblock; red velvet, very worn on outside and spine almost lost, 
                           but with well-preserved turn-ins including a border of plain canvas with a green stripe; no surviving decoration; traces of 
                           two strap-and-pin fastenings with straps of red textile (lost) running from front fore-edge to lost pins near centre of back cover. 
                           The edges of both textblock and boards are gilt (very worn), evidently gilded after binding</p>
                     </binding>
